bout 8 units per period, reaching about 80 by the end. On day 18 a batch of 148 hits the 196-unit cap and about 36 units are lost. Shortages fall to about 5 units, but there are 161 more units bought and extra holding.\n- Net for product 0: +66 units sold × 19 − 161 × 6 − about 330 holding ≈ roughly zero between candidates 0 and 1.\n- Ordering 25–30% above forecast on product 0 (candidates 5 and 7) loses money: almost all the extra units go to waste, overflow or holding.\n\n**4. Product 1 decides it.** Candidate 0 orders exactly the forecast; candidate 1 orders 5% less. The extra 29 units are almost all sold: 14 × 26 − 8 × 29 − about 47 holding ≈ +85 in favour of candidate 0. Candidate 5 (about 10% below forecast) and candidate 7 (about 14% above) are both worse on this product.\n\n**How sure this is:** the expected-value order comes out roughly 0 ≥ 1 > 4 ≈ 6 > the rest. The two leaders are within estimate error of each other, so another analysis could reasonably pick candidate 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 361, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5807, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 361}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:24:29.526Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAoBKr5sPDSeEmzuG7Lg"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01673WWXSdLZcfdZ2uoWnznT", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_0